00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:44.790
A covered call overlay, as the financial post laid out, lets you collect premium on shares

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:48.230
you already own, while you cap the upside in a choppy tape.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:53.170
Rate hike uncertainty is exactly when that cash flow tilt gets more interesting for

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:55.650
a Canadian account that needs income without a sale.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:01.550
One clean way to run it is to buy a broad Canadian equity ETF inside a tax-free savings

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:08.590
account, or TFSA, and sell monthly out-of-the-money calls against it, targeting 1-2% in premium

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:09.250
each month.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:13.470
Think of those calls like renting out a parking spot on land you still own.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:17.990
You keep the lot, you collect rent while it sits, and you give up the right to the

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:20.790
parking fee spike if a concert suddenly fills the block.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:26.170
That structure has historically done its best work in sideways or mildly bullish markets,

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:30.470
where volatility stays high enough to pay you, but the underlying does not rip.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.870
The main risk is opportunity cost.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:37.630
If the market rallies hard, the shares get called away and you watch the rest of the move

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.470
from the sidelines.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:44.830
It works best when the ETF itself shows moderate volatility, enough to support those premiums,

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.550
Not so much that the downside is a different problem.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:53.870
Monthly paying eye shares funds listed on the TSX or SIBOE Canada can sit underneath that

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:58.890
overlay so the coupon and the premium land in the same tax-free account and can be put

00:02:58.890 --> 00:02:59.650
back to work.

00:03:00.451 --> 00:03:05.091
I have no financial relationship with BlackRock or with any of the platforms I named today.

00:03:05.591 --> 00:03:07.171
They are just the tools on the desk.

00:03:07.671 --> 00:03:12.531
Write the 1% to 2% premium target on the order ticket before you click, because a covered

00:03:12.531 --> 00:03:15.691
call without a number is just a hope with an expiry date.

00:03:16.532 --> 00:03:22.792
General Motors is the simulated weekly hold, ticker GM on the NYSE, a consumer cyclical

00:03:22.792 --> 00:03:27.392
earning surprise setup into the next report, and this is a simulated trade for learning

00:03:27.392 --> 00:03:28.992
purposes with no real money.

00:03:29.492 --> 00:03:33.652
The catalyst is the scheduled print that can reprise sentiment across auto-demand.

00:03:33.992 --> 00:03:39.552
The invalidation is an earnings miss of more than 5% versus consensus, or guidance cut

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.232
on North American auto-demand.

00:03:41.232 --> 00:03:45.192
that line gets written before a single simulated dollar is at risk.

00:03:45.572 --> 00:03:51.072
The technical check is a daily close near the 50-day moving average, with the 14-day RSI

00:03:51.072 --> 00:03:55.172
at 48, neither overbought nor oversold, and average volume.

00:03:55.632 --> 00:04:02.332
The stop sits 6% below entry, which on the $1,000 simulated ticket is about $60, and the

00:04:02.332 --> 00:04:08.252
target band is plus 3% to plus 6% if the beat lands and the auto commentary stays constructive.

00:04:08.252 --> 00:04:08.352
narrative.

00:04:08.992 --> 00:04:10.092
Confidence is medium.

00:04:10.752 --> 00:04:15.032
The earnings data is locked, but rotation into consumer names is still a live question.

00:04:15.712 --> 00:04:21.012
Blackberry was a valuation screen on a software name already in a sector rotation, and that

00:04:21.012 --> 00:04:22.752
is not the setup I am repeating here.

00:04:23.781 --> 00:04:25.041
GM is a different family.

00:04:25.621 --> 00:04:30.641
Earning surprise, not a discounted software tape, and the RSI check is there, so we do not

00:04:30.641 --> 00:04:33.601
walk into a name that is already extended in either direction.

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:38.921
The software volume rule from that last hold does not bind this ticker, but the habit

00:04:38.921 --> 00:04:39.221
does.

00:04:39.821 --> 00:04:44.001
Define the data point that kills the thesis, then live with it after the print instead

00:04:44.001 --> 00:04:45.141
of rewriting the story.

00:04:46.024 --> 00:04:51.684
We hold this as shares for five sessions from entry, stop or horizon, no discretionary wiggle,

00:04:52.144 --> 00:04:55.124
and we will mark it against the NASDAQ over that same window.

00:04:55.584 --> 00:04:57.704
If the miss threshold hits, we are out.

00:04:58.144 --> 00:05:02.924
If the beat hits and the commentary holds, we let the target band do the work rather than

00:05:02.924 --> 00:05:04.524
inventing a new reason to stay.

00:05:05.044 --> 00:05:09.504
Copy the invalidation sentence onto your own pad, even if you never touched this name.

00:05:10.064 --> 00:05:11.764
That is the habit, not the ticker.

00:05:12.716 --> 00:05:19.736
Blackberry on the TSX, tickerbb.to, was the last simulated weekly hold, a valuation screen

00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:24.376
on a software name that had raised revenue guidance and was trading at a discount to recent

00:05:24.376 --> 00:05:24.716
growth.

00:05:25.276 --> 00:05:33.316
We simulated buying it at $11.97 Canadian on the Tuesday open and exiting at $11.54 on

00:05:33.316 --> 00:05:41.096
the Monday clothes, six calendar days of market data. That is a loss of 3.59% or $35.92

00:05:41.396 --> 00:05:47.296
on the $1,000 ticket. The NASDAQ composite rose modestly over that same six-day window,

00:05:47.696 --> 00:05:53.016
so on an alpha basis, this was a loss, not a scratch. The valuation math looks stable

00:05:53.016 --> 00:05:58.336
on paper and then failed once broader software rotation accelerated. This didn't work, and

00:05:58.336 --> 00:06:03.136
And next time I would not enter a valuation-driven software name already in a sector rotation,

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:06.136
unless volume is already above the 20-day average.

00:06:06.736 --> 00:06:12.056
Rule, require volume above the 20-day average before entering any valuation-driven software

00:06:12.056 --> 00:06:14.016
name already in a sector rotation.

00:06:14.869 --> 00:06:20.149
BlackRock Canada's eye shares distribution tool is a free monthly list on their site that

00:06:20.149 --> 00:06:25.709
